WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.000
The map shows recorded observations inside the selected geographic and UTC window. Nearby detections are not a validated assignment to an incident.

2
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:04.000
The timeline compares recorded activity within the study. An occupied cell-day counts one detected common cell on one UTC date.

3
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:06.000
These source states distinguish collected records from unknown evidence and processing gaps. An empty record does not establish a fire-free day.

4
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.000
The cited result comes from frozen evidence. Its interpretation remains editable and does not change the source measurements.

5
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Original satellite observations retain native source fields and acquisition time. Those rows and common-cell counts answer different questions.

6
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.000
The study supports inspection of dated thermal observations. It does not establish ignition, continuous spread, a perimeter, or a forecast.
